{
  "@context": "https://doi.org/10.5063/schema/codemeta-2.0",
  "@type": "SoftwareSourceCode",
  "identifier": "MaxMin",
  "description": "Selects a maximally dispersed subset of a fixed set of candidate items under the Max-Min Diversity Problem (MMDP, the discrete p-dispersion objective): maximise the minimum pairwise distance within the chosen subset. Provides a tiered toolbox that operates on a distance matrix, on Euclidean coordinates without materialising the distance matrix, or on an on-demand distance-column oracle for spaces with no coordinate embedding: deterministic Gonzalez farthest-first selection (Gonzalez 1985) <doi:10.1016/0304-3975(85)90224-5> with a choice of peripheral seeding strategies and a robust ensemble default, the DropAdd tabu-search heuristic (Porumbel, Hao & Glover 2011) <doi:10.1007/s10479-011-0898-z>, an exact node-packing integer program (Sayyady & Fathi 2016) <doi:10.1016/j.ejor.2016.02.026>, a GRASP with path-relinking heuristic (Resende, Marti, Gallego & Duarte 2010) <doi:10.1016/j.cor.2008.05.011>, and a local-search polish.",
  "name": "MaxMin: Maximum-Minimum Diversity and Dispersion Subset Selection",
